(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be implemented by individuals or groups, academics, Women and Children advocates, community-based integrated Child protection, community organizations/community institutions/religious institutions/other legitimate institutions.

Article 3
This Regional Regulation aims to:
a. serve as a guideline in the planning and implementation of Women and Children Protection policies;
b. prevent violations of the rights of Women and Children;
c. realize integrated, comprehensive and sustainable Women and Children Protection efforts;
d. prevent decisions and policies that violate and do not support Women and Children Protection efforts; and
e. enhance the role of the Regency Government, community, and other community institutions in Women and Children Protection efforts.

Article 26
(1) The Regency Government is obligated and responsible to:
a. implement the Protection of Women and Children;
b. undertake prevention efforts against acts of violence toward Women and Children; and
c. guarantee the fulfillment of the rights of Women and Children as referred to in Article 5 through Article 25.
(2) The obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may be implemented through:
a. the policy on the Protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence as stipulated by the central government;
b. establishing programs and activities for the Protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence;
c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of the Protection of Women and Children;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of the Protection of Women and Children;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of the Protection of Women and Children in accordance with the Regency's financial capacity;
f. fostering and supervising the implementation of the Protection of Women and Children;
g. establishing an integrated service center; and
h. realizing a Child-Friendly Regency.
(3) The Regency Government as referred to in paragraph (1), shall establish programs and action activities for the Protection of Women and Children in 1 (one) Regional Action Plan as the basis for the Agency to implement the Protection of Women and Children from acts of Violence.
(4) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (3), constitutes part of the RPJMD.
(5) Provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

