Article 2
The Implementation of Protection of Women and Children is based on the principles of:
a. respect and recognition of equal rights and human dignity;
b. non-discrimination;
c. gender equality and justice;
d. protection of human rights of Women and Children;
e. appreciation of the views of Children;
f. best interests of victims of violence; and
g. legal certainty.

CONCERNING
THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF MUSI RAWAS UTARA.
Considering : a. that all forms of violence, torture or treatment that degrades the degree, dignity of women and children constitute violations of human rights, therefore it is necessary to protect their honor and dignity and guarantee their right to life in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
b. that violence, torture or treatment that degrades the degree and dignity of women and children continues to increase so that protection efforts must be carried out;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Protection of Women and Children;
In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 16 of 2013 concerning the Establishment of Musi Rawas Utara Regency in South Sumatra Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2013 Number 112, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5429);
